WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.429
<v Alex Chen>Daniel, good to hear from you — hope the fiscal year turnover wasn't too chaotic.</v>

00:00:07.129 --> 00:00:16.557
<v Daniel Okafor>It's been busy, but good news — budget for data infrastructure got approved for Q4. I want to pick this back up.</v>

00:00:17.257 --> 00:00:24.114
<v Alex Chen>Great timing, we're ready when you are. What would be most useful as a next step?</v>

00:00:24.814 --> 00:00:43.243
<v Daniel Okafor>Two things. First, can you send updated pricing that includes the HIPAA and BAA add-on we discussed with Lena? Second, I'd like to bring a broader group in for a live demo — a couple of engineers who'd actually be building the interfaces.</v>

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:59.371
<v Alex Chen>Both easy. I'll get pricing to you by end of week — anything change on scope since the deep dive, or is it still the two new regional clinic interfaces plus the existing HL7 engine replacement?</v>

00:01:00.071 --> 00:01:11.214
<v Daniel Okafor>Same scope, maybe slightly larger — we just confirmed a third clinic is coming online in Q1, so it might be worth pricing for that too.</v>

00:01:11.914 --> 00:01:23.914
<v Alex Chen>Good to know, I'll include options for that. For the broader demo, does the first week of October work? I can bring Devon back in to run it.</v>

00:01:24.614 --> 00:01:30.614
<v Daniel Okafor>First week works, I'll get invites out to my team once you send times.</v>

00:01:31.314 --> 00:01:39.886
<v Alex Chen>I'll follow up with pricing and time options within the next couple of days. Glad to have this moving again.</v>

00:01:40.586 --> 00:01:44.871
<v Daniel Okafor>Likewise, appreciate you staying in touch while we were stuck.</v>
